---
import TopBar from '../components/TopBar.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy · azuline" description="What the azuline browser extension and this website collect, and where it goes.">
  <div class="screen">
    <TopBar />
    <main class="doc">
      <h1 class="display">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Updated 18 October 2026.</p>

      <h2>The browser extension</h2>
      <p>
        When you save an image, the extension reads the image address, the page address and title, and the artist's name, post title and
        licence if the page shows them. It downloads the image from the site that hosts it.
      </p>
      <p>
        The image and these details go only to the azuline app on the same computer, through the address 127.0.0.1. Nothing is sent to us
        or to anyone else. The extension has no analytics, no ads and no account.
      </p>
      <p>
        The extension keeps a few things in the browser, in storage that only the extension can read: the pairing key from the app, the board you chose, your
        settings, your last five saves, and images that are waiting for the app to open. Removing the extension deletes all of them.
      </p>
      <p>
        On pixiv, the extension adds pixiv's address as the referrer when it downloads an image, because pixiv's image server refuses
        requests without one. It doesn't change any other request.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        azuline.app sets no cookies and has no analytics. It remembers your light or dark choice in your browser's local storage. The site is
        hosted on Cloudflare Pages, so Cloudflare handles each request, including your IP address, to deliver the page. Their
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">privacy policy</a> covers that part.
      </p>

      <h2>The desktop app</h2>
      <p>The app isn't released yet. This page will cover it before the first download goes up.</p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
    </main>
    <footer class="foot"></footer>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .doc {
    width: min(680px, 100%);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: clamp(40px, 8vh, 96px) 0 64px;
  }
  .doc h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
  }
  .doc .lede {
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  .doc h2 {
    margin: 44px 0 0;
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .doc p {
    margin: 14px 0 0;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .doc a {
    color: var(--link);
  }
</style>
